{"actor":{"display":"Evin Tunador","id":"evintunador@gmail.com","type":"human"},"content":{"blocks":[{"content":"1\t# Watches the target CLIs' npm releases and flags when they move outside the\n2\t# version prefixes the fabrication adapters were validated against\n3\t# (docs/specs/ are reverse-engineered and version-pinned by design).\n4\t#\n5\t# Stage 1 (active): daily check → open/update a pinned tracking issue.\n6\t# Stage 2 (commented): hand the issue to a Claude Code action run that\n7\t# re-verifies the spec against the new release and drafts a revalidation PR.\n8\t# Enabling stage 2 needs an ANTHROPIC_API_KEY repo secret — see the TODO.\n9\tname: adapter-drift\n10\ton:\n11\t  schedule:\n12\t    - cron: \"17 6 * * *\"\n13\t  workflow_dispatch: {}\n14\t\n15\tpermissions:\n16\t  contents: read\n17\t  issues: write\n18\t\n19\tjobs:\n20\t  check:\n21\t    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n22\t    outputs:\n23\t      drift: ${{ steps.drift.outputs.drift }}\n24\t      report: ${{ steps.drift.outputs.report }}\n25\t    steps:\n26\t      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n27\t      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n28\t        with:\n29\t          node-version: 22\n30\t      - id: drift\n31\t        run: node scripts/check-adapter-drift.mjs || [ $? -eq 2 ]\n32\t\n33\t  file-issue:\n34\t    needs: check\n35\t    if: needs.check.outputs.drift == 'true'\n36\t    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n37\t    permissions:\n38\t      issues: write\n39\t    steps:\n40\t      - uses: actions/github-script@v7\n41\t        env:\n42\t          REPORT: ${{ needs.check.outputs.report }}\n43\t        with:\n44\t          script: |\n45\t            const title = \"Adapter drift: target CLI released outside validated version range\";\n46\t            const open = await github.rest.issues.listForRepo({\n47\t              ...context.repo, state: \"open\", labels: \"adapter-drift\",\n48\t            });\n49\t            const body = process.env.REPORT +\n50\t              \"\\n\\n_Automated by .github/workflows/adapter-drift.yml — updates daily while drift persists._\";\n51\t            if (open.data.length > 0) {\n52\t              await github.rest.issues.update({\n53\t                ...context.repo, issue_number: open.data[0].number, body,\n54\t              });\n55\t            } else {\n56\t              await github.rest.issues.create({\n57\t                ...context.repo, title, body, labels: [\"adapter-drift\"],\n58\t              });\n59\t            }\n60\t\n61\t  # TODO(stage 2): agent-drafted revalidation PR. Uncomment once an\n62\t  # ANTHROPIC_API_KEY secret is configured and the repo is comfortable letting\n63\t  # CI push branches. The agent re-reads the pinned spec, diffs it against the\n64\t  # new CLI release's session format, and opens a draft PR (spec amendments +\n65\t  # VALIDATED_VERSION_PREFIX bump) or reports that a human is needed.\n66\t  #\n67\t  # draft-pr:\n68\t  #   needs: [check, file-issue]\n69\t  #   if: needs.check.outputs.drift == 'true'\n70\t  #   runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n71\t  #   permissions:\n72\t  #     contents: write\n73\t  #     pull-requests: write\n74\t  #   steps:\n75\t  #     - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n76\t  #     - uses: anthropics/claude-code-action@v1\n77\t  #       with:\n78\t  #         anthropic_api_key: ${{ secrets.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY }}\n79\t  #         prompt: |\n80\t  #           ${{ needs.check.outputs.report }}\n81\t  #\n82\t  #           Install the drifted CLI release(s), re-verify the fabrication\n83\t  #           spec(s) named above against them (headless probes only), amend\n84\t  #           the spec docs and VALIDATED_VERSION_PREFIX if the format is\n85\t  #           unchanged, run `npm test`, and open a DRAFT pull request with\n86\t  #           your findings. If the format changed materially, do not guess:\n87\t  #           open the PR with the spec diff annotated as needing human\n88\t  #           validation via `npm run smoke:interactive`.\n89\t","tool_use_id":"toolu_01DKaymso6Jjykb8xrNxe2Wp","type":"tool